{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing i64 = long long;\nusing u64 = unsigned long long;\nusing pii = pair<int, int>;\nusing pll = pair<i64, i64>;\n\nconstexpr int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint n, S, cnt[250], id[250];\nint f[10][250];\nvector<int> vec[10];\nunordered_map<i64, int> memo;\n\nint modPow(int b, int e) {\n    int r = 1;\n    b %= MOD;\n    while (e) {\n        if (e & 1) r = (1LL * r * b) % MOD;\n        b = (1LL * b * b) % MOD;\n        e >>= 1;\n    }\n    return r;\n}\n\nint dfs(int pos, u64 state) {\n    if (!state) return 0;\n    if (pos == n) return 1;\n    \n    u64 key = (static_cast<u64>(pos) << 32) ^ state;\n    if (memo.count(key)) return memo[key];\n    \n    ++S;\n    int res = 0;\n    \n    for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n        u64 nxt = 0;\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < vec[pos].size(); ++idx) {\n            if (!(state & (1ULL << idx))) continue;\n            int prevMask = vec[pos][idx];\n            for (int bit = 0; bit < n; ++bit) {\n                if ((mask & (1 << bit)) && !(prevMask & (1 << bit))) {\n                    nxt |= 1ULL << id[prevMask | (1 << bit)];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        res = (res + 1LL * f[pos][mask] * dfs(pos + 1, nxt)) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    return memo[key] = res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n;\n    int inv100 = modPow(100, MOD - 2);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        f[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int P;\n            cin >> P;\n            int p1 = (1LL * P * inv100) % MOD;\n            int p0 = (1 + MOD - p1) % MOD;\n            for (int k = 0; k < (1 << j); ++k) {\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (1LL * f[i][k] * p1) % MOD;\n                f[i][k] = (1LL * f[i][k] * p0) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n        cnt[i] = __builtin_popcount(i);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n        vec[cnt[i]].push_back(i);\n        id[i] = vec[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n    }\n    \n    cout << dfs(0, 1) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom functools import lru_cache\n\nsys.setrecursionlimit(10000)\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mod_pow(b, e):\n    r = 1\n    b %= MOD\n    while e:\n        if e & 1:\n            r = (r * b) % MOD\n        b = (b * b) % MOD\n        e >>= 1\n    return r\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    inv100 = mod_pow(100, MOD - 2)\n    \n    f = [[0] * (1 << n) for _ in range(n)]\n    idx = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        f[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(n):\n            P = int(data[idx])\n            idx += 1\n            p1 = (P * inv100) % MOD\n            p0 = (1 + MOD - p1) % MOD\n            for k in range(1 << j):\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (f[i][k] * p1) % MOD\n                f[i][k] = (f[i][k] * p0) % MOD\n    \n    cnt = [0] * (1 << n)\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        cnt[i] = bin(i).count('1')\n    \n    vec = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    id_map = [0] * (1 << n)\n    \n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        vec[cnt[i]].append(i)\n        id_map[i] = len(vec[cnt[i]]) - 1\n    \n    memo = {}\n    \n    def dfs(pos, state):\n        if not state:\n            return 0\n        if pos == n:\n            return 1\n        \n        key = (pos << 32) ^ state\n        if key in memo:\n            return memo[key]\n        \n        res = 0\n        for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n            nxt = 0\n            for idx_val in range(len(vec[pos])):\n                if not (state & (1 << idx_val)):\n                    continue\n                prev_mask = vec[pos][idx_val]\n                for bit in range(n):\n                    if (mask & (1 << bit)) and not (prev_mask & (1 << bit)):\n                        nxt |= 1 << id_map[prev_mask | (1 << bit)]\n            res = (res + f[pos][mask] * dfs(pos + 1, nxt)) % MOD\n        \n        memo[key] = res\n        return res\n    \n    print(dfs(0, 1))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0002101439022226259, -5.960462772236497e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.0004210777406115085, -0.0002330270071979612, -0.000266278104390949, -0.20457245409488678, -0.20473897457122803, -8.940656698541716e-06, -0.0001512651506345719, -3.9457496313843876e-05, -8.654219709569588e-05, -0.00013517419574782252, -0.20203641057014465, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -0.00011991735664196312, -2.253030106658116e-05, -2.276871418871451e-05, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.00022671037004329264, -0.0002727136597968638, -0.000164018536452204, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.168244216387393e-05, -0.3133033215999603, -0.03813860937952995, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07